STR_2465: huffstr "Make that invitation at the House, where Mara can judge the place being offered rather than the idea of it."
STR_2446: huffstr "Mara accepts the thanks without waving it away. You held your side of the mechanism, she says. So did I. That is worth saying plainly once."
STR_2464: huffstr "Mara already chose to use the House as a base. Her pack remains where she placed it in the Attic; repeating the invitation does not make the choice more binding."
STR_2473: huffstr "Mara already has the pack on her own shoulder."
STR_2406: huffstr "Mara cannot honestly claim that history yet. Let her witness it, measure it, read it, or hold the evidence first."
STR_2502: huffstr "Mara chooses her own footing. Ask her to follow, wait, or help with the actual mechanism rather than steering her by compass point."
STR_2409: huffstr "Mara closes her notebook. As far as the Dam survey takes us, she says. Do not mistake that for an oath to follow you into every hole in the Empire."
STR_2462: huffstr "Mara considers you for a moment. We have not even finished one honest field entry together, she says. A permanent-sounding invitation would be theater."
STR_2412: huffstr "Mara crosses the threshold, then stops—not at the treasure, but at the signs that the House has been repaired, damaged, used, and returned to. So this is the base, she says."
STR_2422: huffstr "Mara crouches beside the jar without touching it. Broad tail, pale impact line, faster-water body, she says. The lowered reservoir changed more than the view."
STR_2503: huffstr "Mara declines to become a remote inventory hand. Name the shared physical task or keep custody yourself."
STR_2480: huffstr "Mara declines to turn food into a shortcut around the unfinished invitation. Settle the question of whether she is actually using the House first."
STR_2509: huffstr "Mara does not accept permanent custody merely because an object was offered. SHOW it to her if the point is evidence; keep it if the point is ownership."
STR_2466: huffstr "Mara does not answer immediately. Then: I would consider using the House as a base. But my field pack is still at the Dam. We do not make a new life by pretending the old one teleported. Come back with me; at the Dam Base, ask me to take my pack."
STR_2512: huffstr "Mara does not flinch, but she does not meet you halfway. Not at a working dam, not as payment for competence, and not before we know what this is, she says. The boundary is calm and complete."
STR_2384: huffstr "Mara glances from the river to the dam face. Diagnose the mechanism, let me brace the panel, and we can make one trustworthy record between us."
STR_2381: huffstr "Mara glances toward the Attic where she chose to leave her field pack. I am using the House as a base, she says. Using is not owning, and staying is not surrendering my route."
STR_2488: huffstr "Mara glances toward the route back to the House, then at you. The Attic is a base, not a leash, she says. Choose the expedition; ask me to follow if our routes overlap."
STR_2445: huffstr "Mara has already heard you. Repetition does not turn gratitude into currency."
STR_2436: huffstr "Mara has measurements but no jointly witnessed load change. Arm the interlock, have her brace the panel, and cycle the real gates before filing a conclusion."
STR_2403: huffstr "Mara has no earned knowledge of your House yet. She does not promote a claim to geography merely because someone says it confidently."
STR_2463: huffstr "Mara has not seen the House. She will not agree to live inside a description."
STR_2421: huffstr "Mara holds the panel steady, but the bolt does not transfer force. Check the yellow interlock before trying to persuade the wrench."
STR_2444: huffstr "Mara inclines her head. Save the serious thanks for after the machinery has given us a reason, she says."
STR_2404: huffstr "Mara is a route historian by vocation and a field surveyor by necessity. Her work predates meeting you and will continue whenever your routes divide."
STR_2489: huffstr "Mara is here as company, not a replacement command prompt. Ask what she thinks or choose a route and ask her to follow."
STR_2461: huffstr "Mara is not here to accept or refuse the invitation."
STR_2407: huffstr "Mara is not here to make that decision."
STR_2470: huffstr "Mara is not here to take custody of her pack."
STR_2485: huffstr "Mara is not leading a sightseeing tour. Complete the shared Dam work before assuming her route is yours."
STR_2433: huffstr "Mara is not physically present to make the second set of observations."
STR_2419: huffstr "Mara keeps both hands against the shuddering panel while the bolt turns. When the deeper machinery takes the load, she does not celebrate; she watches the stone, counts the delay, and says, Again, but now we know which part of the map was lying."
STR_2498: huffstr "Mara keeps custody of her own field equipment. Ask for help with a real task rather than treating her as an equipment locker."
STR_2468: huffstr "Mara keeps the pack on her shoulder. The Living Room is shared traffic, not private camp. Show me the Attic, she says. If it is sound, ask again there."
STR_2475: huffstr "Mara kneels at the waxed pack, checks the notebook seal, coils the loose camp cord, and shoulders the weight herself. Nothing changes custody: the pack was hers at the Dam and is hers on the road. All right, she says. Now we can see whether your House can hold a second route without swallowing it."
STR_2471: huffstr "Mara leaves the pack where it is. I still have field work based here, she says. Give me a reason to move camp before turning it into luggage."
STR_2379: huffstr "Mara listens to the water behind the wall. Conversation can wait until the pipe stops trying to become a river."
STR_2380: huffstr "Mara looks around the House as someone who has begun using it rather than visiting it. We have a Dam record, a moved camp, and one meal that actually existed, she says. That is enough history to stop calling this accidental company."
STR_2467: huffstr "Mara looks toward her pack. If I am going to choose a place for it, I need to be carrying it there myself."
STR_2511: huffstr "Mara looks toward the stair to the Attic, then back at you. Letting my pack live here was a choice about shelter, she says. Do not turn it into a claim on me."
STR_2411: huffstr "Mara marks the location in her notebook. I will wait here, she says, not everywhere and not forever."
STR_2455: huffstr "Mara must be physically beside you in the Cellar to work the upper bar."
STR_2427: huffstr "Mara must be physically present to hold the other side."
STR_2479: huffstr "Mara must be physically present to share the meal."
STR_2430: huffstr "Mara plants one boot against the stone curb and braces the control panel at its load-bearing edge. Turn the bolt with the wrench, she says. If the yellow interlock is armed, I can keep the panel from walking while the gates take the force."
STR_2486: huffstr "Mara points up toward the control face. Her current work leads north and up to the Dam, but she waits for you to choose the movement yourself."
STR_2429: huffstr "Mara refuses to brace an undiagnosed machine. Examine the control panel and establish what is actually connected first."
STR_2410: huffstr "Mara refuses to wait inside a flooding maintenance room. She retreats through the doorway to the Dam Lobby and waits where the architecture is making fewer threats."
STR_2501: huffstr "Mara refuses. That circuit is scarred, pressurized, and unsupported by a relief path. You may make your own bad decision; you may not issue it as hers."
STR_2413: huffstr "Mara remains outside the flooding maintenance room. Seal it or come back out, she calls."
STR_2450: huffstr "Mara remembers the apology. She is watching the behavior that follows it, not requesting another performance."
STR_2500: huffstr "Mara retains the working original. She will share what it says, but exact custody remains hers until she chooses otherwise."
STR_2408: huffstr "Mara settles the survey rope across her shoulder. For the routes we have actually agreed to share, yes."
STR_2415: huffstr "Mara stays behind. That route is outside the plan you made together; her location remains exactly where you left her."
STR_2513: huffstr "Mara steps back. You have mistaken a shared location for a shared history, she says."
STR_2514: huffstr "Mara steps clear before the action can become force. She is another adventurer, not an obtainable object."
STR_2414: huffstr "Mara stops short of the Troll Room. I do not enter an occupied killing ground merely because you walked first, she says."
STR_2383: huffstr "Mara studies the changed pressure in the stone. We have the mechanism, she says. Now we measure what it actually did."
STR_2423: huffstr "Mara studies the narrow silver body in the jar. River form, steady-current musculature, no fresh gate scar, she says. Record the water state with the animal or the record is decoration."
STR_2416: huffstr "Mara studies the rust around the blue pipe circuit. That line has pressure scars and no credible relief path, she says. Press it if you must, but do not call the result unforeseeable."
STR_2456: huffstr "Mara studies the seam and shakes her head. We have not worked together well enough for me to put my rope where your hands cannot reach, she says."
STR_2441: huffstr "Mara takes enough time to examine the "
STR_2504: huffstr "Mara Tallow is a dark-haired field surveyor in a weathered coat, with a measured rope and hooded lantern carried as her own equipment. She watches routes, load-bearing stone, water marks, and people with the same patient suspicion."
STR_2807: huffstr "Mara Tallow is here with a waxed survey book, watching the route rather than waiting to be assigned one."
STR_2469: huffstr "Mara tests the Attic floorboards, the roofline, the windowless angles, and the distance to the stair before setting down her own field pack. This will do, she says. I am choosing to use the House as a base. The pack stays mine, the room stays yours, and either of us may change the arrangement by saying so. For now, the House contains one more actual life."
STR_2382: huffstr "Mara touches the joint survey sheet inside her coat. The Dam entry is honest, she says. That is rarer than it sounds. When our routes overlap, ask me to come; when they do not, I still have work of my own."
STR_2458: huffstr "Mara uncoils her own measured rope and works its narrow end through the real trap-door seam. You lift from below until the wood takes some of the weight; she feeds the line across the hidden upper bar, catches it, and draws while you keep the door from dropping. The bar scrapes once across the floor above, then comes free."
STR_2448: huffstr "Mara waits for the missing noun. Apologize for what, exactly?"
STR_2420: huffstr "Mara watches the gate state change. The mechanism works, she says, but a witnessed operation is not yet a joint survey."
STR_2424: huffstr "Mara watches the silverfin recover its place in the current. Evidence observed, animal alive, custody closed, she says. That is an unusually clean ending."
STR_2510: huffstr "Mara's expression warms, but she does not meet you halfway. A shared base and a shared meal are history, she says, not permission to skip the history that has not happened yet."
STR_2472: huffstr "Mara's field camp is at the Dam Base. She cannot pack a camp from a different room."
STR_2487: huffstr "Mara's next route depends on the evidence: west to compare reservoir state, north to the maintenance controls, or south toward the older passages. She will not choose your investigation for you."
STR_2496: huffstr "Mara's rope is waxed against water, marked at measured intervals, and coiled for use rather than decoration."
STR_2806: huffstr "Mara's waxed canvas field pack is secured with a surveyor's locking hitch."
